<title>USA: Great Northern Iron cuts payout to $1.50/shr.</title>
<headline>Great Northern Iron cuts payout to $1.50/shr.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Northern Iron Ore Properties said Monday it would pay a first quarter 1997 distribution of $1.50 a share, down from $1.70 paid in January.</p>
<p>The first-quarter 1996 payout was $1.35 a share.</p>
<p>The current distribution will be paid on April 30 to shareholders of record on March 31.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
